+/*
+ * Cinecore (macOS): zero-copy GPU sharing between wined3d (OpenGL) and DXMT (Metal) through IOSurface.
+ *
+ * Metal shared textures (newSharedTextureWithDescriptor) are backed by GPU-private IOSurfaces that OpenGL
+ * cannot bind. For the frames that madVR renders in Direct3D 9 and presents in Direct3D 11, the application
+ * creates a linear 64-bit half-float IOSurface first (cinecore_surface_create); the next shared RGBA16Float
+ * Metal texture of that size is then created on it (method swizzling on the Metal classes), its shared handle
+ * carries the IOSurface mach port and opening it on another MTLDevice gives a texture on the same IOSurface.
+ * On the wined3d CS thread the IOSurface is bound to a rectangle texture (CGLTexImageIOSurface2D) and the
+ * frame is copied there with glBlitFramebuffer: no readback to system memory, no CPU copy.
+ */
+
